WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.700
We're following

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.401
new details

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.969
about that Chinese spy

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.171
balloon traveling across the country.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:05.972
New video

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.240
in to the CNN NEWSROOM

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.408
showing the balloon now

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.709
hovering over

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.312
Asheville and Charlotte, North Carolina,

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.680
in the last hour.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.415
And it could make it out to sea

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.883
at any moment.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.151
The balloon was first

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.620
spotted over Montana on Wednesday.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.788
China claims

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.757
it's a civilian research vessel

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.925
that blew off course, but the U.S.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:26.926
isn't buying that.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.095
Calling the balloons flight over U.S.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.531
soil an irresponsible act.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.033
Secretary of State

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.434
Antony Blinken

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.002
postponing a planned trip

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.104
to Beijing in response.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:38.838
CNN's Oren

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.907
Liebermann is at the Pentagon for us.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.276
So, Oren, officials say the balloon

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.811
doesn't currently currently

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.047
seem to present a threat.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.583
But why is the Pentagon also proceeding

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.518
with caution on it?

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.187
So the Pentagon has said for now

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.822
that it will not be shooting this down

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.357
because of the risks

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.792
from two different perspectives.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.827
First, there's the risk to what's below

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.995
blow something up at

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.063
60,000 feet,

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.397
and that could be scattered over

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.765
quite a large debris field.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.800
So there is a risk

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.168
to people and property

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.536
but they are keeping

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.770
a very close eye on it

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.272
and are continuously monitoring this

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.507
as it makes its way across, frankly,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.875
much of the United States

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.110
almost like a scenic tour

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.244
from the Northwest

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.112
over Montana

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:19.446
to where

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.280
it's just been spotted

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.048
over the course of the last hour or so.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.450
Asheville, North Carolina,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.751
Charlotte, North Carolina,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:25.618
some sightings there.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.787
So it's making its way

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.222
excuse me, along that sort of east

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.590
southeast track.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.124
The other reason

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.459
they haven't taken it down yet

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.359
is because they don't believe

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.360
it has surveillance

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.096
or intelligence gathering capabilities

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.630
above and beyond.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.565
Chinese spy

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.065
satellites,

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.633
which are constantly rotating

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.101
around the earth

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.635
and taking their own pictures

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.570
of the United States.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.771
So for that reason,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.572
the decision has been

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.906
made at this point,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.041
not to, frankly,

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.576
shoot this thing out of the sky.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.477
President Joe Biden

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.245
did request military options

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.347
when this was first spotted over the U.S.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.249
earlier this week over Montana.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.617
But the Pentagon recommended

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.052
against that at this time.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:01:59.886
The question is,

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.855
what is the response from here?

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:02.989
Both the State Department

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.624
and the Pentagon have made it clear

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.693
they view this as a violation of U.S.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.494
airspace,

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.028
a violation of breach

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.463
of international law.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.297
And they view this

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.666
severely ahead of a high stakes visit

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.534
or planned visit,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.202
I should say, of Secretary of State

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.238
Antony Blinken to Beijing

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.006
it was to be the first time the top U.S.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.041
diplomat has visited China and Beijing

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.343
in six years,

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.144
and the Chinese took

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.678
this very seriously,

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.447
especially with high tensions.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.482
So for this to have happened,

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.651
a major mistake on their part,

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.853
and they have apologized multiple times

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:34.721
and said, look,

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.157
this was just a weather balloon

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.658
that was barely controllable.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.860
It was pulled over the U.S. by winds.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.261
The U.S.

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:41.861
has made it clear

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.963
they're not buying that explanation.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.965
They delayed or postponed

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.535
at least the trip of Blinken to China

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.736
And now the question,

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.904
where does this go from here?

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.739
First, is there more diplomatic fallout?

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.306
Second,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.141
is there a military response

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.609
in being at the Pentagon today?

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.977
There are key staff members

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.679
from the top levels of the Pentagon here.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.080
And that raises the question.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.915
Does the Pentagon plan

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:02.715
on shooting this down

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.584
once there's no longer a risk of

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.919
the people and property below?

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.821
And this is out over U.S. waters right?

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.489
All right.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.491
Well, you'll be watching. Keep us posted.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.326
Oren Liebermann, thank you so much.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.427
I mean, so many extraordinary

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.395
things about this,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.763
but particularly the balloon

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.231
is actually visible

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.399
to the naked eye,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.367
giving many in North Carolina

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.502
a view this morning.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.269
And joining us right now

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.138
on the phone, Evan Fisher.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.973
He saw the balloon over Asheville,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.608
North Carolina, this morning.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.077
Evan, had you been looking for it?

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.579
I mean, in anticipation

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.614
that it might be moving over

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.083
North Carolina airspace?

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.051
How did you spot it?

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:39.452
Well,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.220
we were expecting it

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:40.954
to move over

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.355
the western North Carolina area

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.557
between 2 a.m. and 6 a.m..

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.992
But then to our surprise,

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.228
it didn't show up until after sunrise.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.596
So I spotted it around

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.297
eight 50 this morning

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.232
in the southern sky

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.167
to the south of Asheville

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.369
and much larger than I expected it to be,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.303
drifting off

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.304
to the east southeast,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.138
as we were just talking

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.540
about an interview.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.608
Beautiful sight,

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:02.942
a little unusual

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:03.943
as a member of the public.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:04.177
You know,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.645
we're not too educated on

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.779
everything that is going on

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.380
with the balloon.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.649
But it was very interesting to see it

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.650
and follow the saga

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.451
that's been playing out

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.418
across the United States

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.653
over the past few days.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.654
And these are your images

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.588
we're looking at, right?

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.889
I mean, you saw it with the naked eye,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.791
but then how did you get these images?

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.892
Is this from your,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:20.860
you know, your cell phone

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.263
or did you use a camera,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.832
a professional grade camera?

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.299
Sure.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.533
So for the still image

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.802
that was with a camera and a zoom lens,

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.870
that was pretty tight

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.372
on the balloon itself.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.673
And with some editing and cropping,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:34.507
I was able to get it

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.942
pretty close on there.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.743
But for the video

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.077
that was actually just shot with

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.579
with an iPhone zoomed in.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.680
And as you can see

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.347
from the very beginning,

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.782
it does look small on

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.851
iPhone photos and iPhone videos.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.785
But in reality,

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.487
it looks much larger in person

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.421
to the naked eye.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.156
Wow. And here you're a meteorologist.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:51.124
You've got a clear sky.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.393
She had a clear viewing of it.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.962
What are ordinary people

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.164
in your proximity saying about this site?

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.433
Oh, the community was very excited

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.301
to be able to contribute

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.902
to these reports.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:03.703
There were lots of folks

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.038
all across Asheville up

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:05.972
to South Carolina

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.939
and western North Carolina

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.740
as a whole,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.808
sending in pictures

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.575
and just sharing their

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.077
experience with it.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:11.844
And that was so wonderful

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.146
to see everyone coming together

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.515
and then sharing oh, yeah.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:16.449
I mean, you mentioned it

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.450
being a beautiful site.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.217
I mean, there's something

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.052
there are a lot of things

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.054
very ominous about this. It's mysterious.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.488
We don't know the purpose of it.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.892
What what it is gaining from,

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.327
you know, being

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:30.196
over the North Carolina skies there.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.864
But talk to me about

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:32.965
just emotionally

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.801
what you were feeling and thinking

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.169
not just as a meteorologist,

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.370
but just as a,

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.906
you know, as a citizen with this

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.842
unknown object in the air and moving.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:44.410
You're absolutely right.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:44.811
It is a bit

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.846
ominous and a little concerning.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.847
But to be honest,

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.349
in western North Carolina,

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.250
I wasn't too concerned about the spy

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.151
aspect of it.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.619
I'm not sure how that would impact

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:54.253
my day to day

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:56.356
life here in Fairview, North Carolina.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.759
But my gut reaction was just excitement.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.194
I really did not expect to see it

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.029
because it was supposed to pass over

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.330
so much earlier in the day.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.498
So when I stepped out on the porch

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.899
and looked up in the sky,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.601
lo and behold, there it was.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.269
And I went scrambling for a camera.

